# Custom Web Fonts with `@font-face` 🌐

Use `@font-face` to load custom font files hosted on your server or CDN:

```css_not
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Inter';
  src: url('/fonts/Inter-Variable.woff2') format('woff2');
  font-weight: 100 900;
  font-display: swap; /* Immediately shows system font while web font downloads */
}
```

## Font Formats:
- **WOFF2 (Web Open Font Format 2):** Best compression and universal modern support. Always prefer `.woff2`!
- `font-display: swap`: Prevents "Flash of Invisible Text" (FOIT) by displaying a fallback font until the custom font is ready.

# Modern Fluid Typography with `clamp()` 🌊

Instead of writing five media queries just to resize text for mobile, tablet, and desktop, use `clamp()`:

```css_not
h1 {
  /* clamp(MINIMUM, PREFERRED, MAXIMUM) */
  font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw + 1rem, 3.5rem);
}
```

## How It Works:
- On tiny mobile screens: font size never drops below `1.75rem`.
- On huge desktop displays: font size never expands past `3.5rem`.
- In between: scales smoothly and fluidly along with viewport width (`4vw`)!

# Line Height (`line-height`) 📖

`line-height` controls the vertical breathing room between lines of text.

```css_not
/* Always use UNITLESS numbers for line-height! */
body {
  line-height: 1.6; /* 1.6 times the current font-size */
}

h1 {
  line-height: 1.2; /* Tight line height for large headings */
}
```

> 🎯 **Typography Golden Rule:** Always use unitless numbers (e.g. `1.6`) instead of pixels or rems. Unitless line heights scale proportionally and inherit accurately when child elements change font size!

# Text Alignment (`text-align`) 🎯

Controls horizontal text alignment within block containers:

```css_not
.left-text   { text-align: left; }
.center-text { text-align: center; }
.right-text  { text-align: right; }
.justify     { text-align: justify; } /* Stretches text to touch both margins */
```

> ⚠️ **Accessibility Warning:** Avoid `text-align: justify` on the web! It creates uneven word gaps ("rivers of white space") that make reading extremely difficult for people with dyslexia.

# Letter Spacing & Word Spacing 🔠

Fine-tune typography rhythm:

```css_not
/* Letter Spacing (Tracking) */
.uppercase-badge {
  text-transform: uppercase;
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em; /* Adds elegant breathing room between caps */
}

.tight-heading {
  letter-spacing: -0.03em; /* Sleek, modern tight tracking for huge hero titles */
}

/* Word Spacing */
p {
  word-spacing: 0.05em;
}
```

# Text Truncation with Ellipsis (...) ✂️

Truncating single-line text that overflows its box:

```css_not
.truncate-single-line {
  white-space: nowrap;        /* Prevents text from wrapping to a new line */
  overflow: hidden;           /* Hides overflow */
  text-overflow: ellipsis;    /* Replaces clipped text with "..." */
  max-width: 200px;
}
```

## Multi-Line Clamping with CSS:
```css_not
.truncate-multiline {
  display: -webkit-box;
  -webkit-line-clamp: 3;      /* Clamps after 3 lines */
  -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
  overflow: hidden;
}
```

# The `font` Shorthand Property 🖌️

Combine multiple font properties into a single declaration:

```css_not
/* Syntax: font: [style] [weight] [size]/[line-height] [family] */
p {
  font: italic bold 1rem/1.6 'Inter', sans-serif;
}
```

> ⚠️ **Shorthand Rule:** When using the `font` shorthand, `font-size` and `font-family` are **mandatory**. If either is missing, the entire declaration is invalid!

# Variable Fonts: Single File, Infinite Styles 🚀

Traditional web fonts require downloading separate files for Regular, Bold, and Italic. A **Variable Font** bundles all weights and styles into a single lightweight file!

```css_not
@font-face {
  font-family: 'RobotoFlex';
  src: url('RobotoFlex-Variable.woff2') format('woff2');
  font-weight: 100 1000;
}

h1 {
  font-family: 'RobotoFlex', sans-serif;
  font-weight: 642; /* Any exact numeric weight from 100 to 1000! */
}
```

# The Magic `ch` Unit for Readability 📏

The `ch` unit represents the width of the `0` (zero) character in the current font.

```css_not
article p {
  max-width: 65ch; /* Perfectly bounds line length for optimal reading rhythm! */
  margin-left: auto;
  margin-right: auto;
}
```

Lines wider than 75-80 characters strain reader eyes when jumping to the next line. `max-width: 65ch` guarantees comfortable readability on any device!

# Typography Depth: `text-shadow` 🌫️

Add subtle glows or drop shadows to text:

```css_not
/* Syntax: text-shadow: [offset-x] [offset-y] [blur-radius] [color] */
.hero-headline {
  color: #ffffff;
  text-shadow: 0 2px 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
}

/* Neon Glow Effect */
.neon-sign {
  color: #00ffcc;
  text-shadow: 0 0 5px #00ffcc, 0 0 20px #00ffcc;
}
```

# Real-World Component: Editorial Article Header 📰

```html_not
<header class="article-header">
  <span class="category-badge">Web Engineering</span>
  <h1 class="headline">Building Scalable Modern Typography</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">A masterclass in responsive font scales, accessibility, and fluid line heights.</p>
</header>
```

```css_not
.article-header {
  max-width: 70ch;
  margin: 40px auto 24px;
}

.category-badge {
  text-transform: uppercase;
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: #2563eb;
}

.headline {
  font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
  font-weight: 800;
  line-height: 1.15;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  color: #0f172a;
  margin: 8px 0 16px;
}

.subtitle {
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  line-height: 1.6;
  color: #64748b;
}
```
